ENTITY action_directive;
  name : label;
  description : OPTIONAL text;
  analysis : text;
  comment : text;
  requests : SET [1:?] OF versioned_action_request;
END_ENTITY;


(*"action_directive"
An *action_directive* is an authoritative instrument that provides directions to achieve the specified results.

[example]
====
ISO Directives Part 3 provides guidance for the development of standards documents within ISO.
====

*)


(*"action_directive.analysis"

an informal description of the results of the analysis that was carried out on the elements of the requests set.
The request sets are the
express_ref:[action_schema.versioned_action_request]s
referenced in the requests attribute.

NOTE: The reason that different requests are satisfied by the *action_directive* could be recorded in this attribute.

*)


(*"action_directive.comment"
an informal description of any other pertinent information.
*)


(*"action_directive.description"
the
express_ref:[support_resource_schema.text]
that characterizes the *action_directive*.
The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"action_directive.name"
the
express_ref:[support_resource_schema.label]
by which the *action_directive* is known.
*)


(*"action_directive.requests"
a set of
express_ref:[action_schema.versioned_action_request]
entity data types that defines the expected results.
*)
